--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2989f6b7554baf142b3f807ffa71cecf, type: 3}
  m_Name: TutorialEntriesContainer
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  tutorialEntries:
  - id: 0
    tutorialEntryText: 'Conductor,

      

      If you are reading this document,
      it means you have been assigned to duty aboard an Interworld Train.

      So
      not ask why it is you.

      Do not ask where this train is truly headed.

      

      Your
      role has been clearly defined..'
  - id: 1
    tutorialEntryText: 'Guard the Harmony.

      Maintain order.

      Ensure
      that every soul reaches where it is meant to go.

      

      The train
      under your care is a Bridge.

      It connects the world of the viking with
      what lies beyond.

      Not all passengers are aware that their journey has
      already ended.'
  - id: 2
    tutorialEntryText: 'Guard the Harmony.

      Maintain order.

      Ensure
      that every soul reaches where it is meant to go.

      

      The train
      under your care is a Bridge.

      It connects the world of the viking with
      what lies beyond.

      Not all passengers are aware that their journey has
      already ended.'
  - id: 3
    tutorialEntryText: 'You are the Conductor.

      

      Not a judge.

      Not
      a savior.

      Not an executioner.

      

      Your task is not to
      pass judgement upon the deeds of the passengers, but to enforce the rules of
      passage.

      Yet remember - every decision you make affects the delicate
      balance of the Train and yourself.'
  - id: 4
    tutorialEntryText: 'Keep in mind -

      Rules exist so that the Train may
      continue its journey.


      During each shift you will:

      walk between
      the carriages of the Train,

      speak with travelers,

      inspect their
      tickets and Life Cards,'
  - id: 5
    tutorialEntryText: 'Each passenger must be verified for:

      ticket validity,

      consistency
      of name and personal data,

      date of passage,

      and any other detected
      anomalies.'
  - id: 6
    tutorialEntryText: 'Remember! Some tickets are issued incorrectly. Others may
      have long expired. There are also passengers who should never have boarded
      the Train at all. All anomalies should be reported to your superiors. '
  - id: 7
    tutorialEntryText: 'The Train operates through Harmony.  Every decision you make
      influences the level of Harmony. And the level of Harmony determines the condition
      of the Train. When Harmony weakens: lights may begin to flicker, music may
      fade or distort, your own memories may begin to blur. '
  - id: 8
    tutorialEntryText: "Every shift leaves a mark.  To occupy your thoughts, our
      Dear Employee, we have provided you with a Conductor\u2019s Journal. You may
      record your thoughts, reflections, and memories within it. Use it freely, it
      is yours alone. It will not be reviewed.. "
  - id: 9
    tutorialEntryText: 'Final note,

      

      Not every story deserves to
      continue.

      Not every soul is ready to reach its destination.

      

      Your
      task is not to mend the world.

      Your task is to keep the Train moving.

      

      Guard
      the Harmony.

      And do not ask too many questions.

      

      *signature*'
